# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining methods {#combining-methods}"
msgstr "Combinación de métodos {#combining-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE relies on the following:\n"
msgstr "ZNE se basa en lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A well-defined noise-scaling parameter $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Un parámetro de escalado del ruido $\\lambda$ bien definido\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sufficiently smooth and predictable scaling of expectation values with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Un escalado de los valores esperados con $\\lambda$ suficientemente suave y predecible\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same effective noise channel, at different strengths\n"
msgstr "El mismo canal de ruido efectivo, con diferentes intensidades\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "No bias introduced that does not scale with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Ningún sesgo introducido que no escale con $\\lambda$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE combines cleanly with techniques that remove non-scaling biases (like M3) or make noise more regular (like twirling), but conflicts with techniques that either attempt to cancel noise entirely (PEC) or reshape it dynamically (DD).\n"
msgstr "ZNE se combina bien con técnicas que eliminan sesgos que no escalan (como M3) o que hacen el ruido más regular (como el twirling), pero entra en conflicto con técnicas que intentan cancelar el ruido por completo (PEC) o remodelarlo dinámicamente (DD).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, M3 addresses only measurement/readout error, which in practice can be treated as separate from gate errors (which are the focus of error scaling processes in ZNE). M3 is largely independent of gate folding; it can be cleanly combined with ZNE. TREX is very similar, and it can be combined with ZNE.\n"
msgstr "En particular, M3 aborda únicamente el error de medición/lectura, que en la práctica puede tratarse como independiente de los errores de las puertas (que son el foco de los procesos de escalado de errores en ZNE). M3 es en gran medida independiente del gate folding; se puede combinar limpiamente con ZNE. TREX es muy similar y se puede combinar con ZNE.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling does focus on gates, unlike M3 and TREX. However, recall that Pauli twirling does not directly mitigate error/noise; rather, it changes it to make it more predictable. Pauli twirling might actually be beneficial to the ZNE process in making gate errors scale more linearly and thus make the extrapolation more accurate.\n"
msgstr "El twirling de Pauli sí se centra en las puertas, a diferencia de M3 y TREX. Sin embargo, recuerda que el twirling de Pauli no mitiga directamente el error/ruido; más bien lo cambia para hacerlo más predecible. El twirling de Pauli podría ser beneficioso para el proceso de ZNE al hacer que los errores de las puertas escalen de forma más lineal y, por tanto, que la extrapolación sea más precisa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dynamical decoupling (DD) is more nuanced. DD dynamically alters noise behavior by partially cancelling certain errors through the addition of gate sequences. If it is possible to construct circuits in such a way that DD behaves the same even when gates or blocks are folded, then in principle one could combine ZNE and DD, but in practice DD sometimes interferes with the scaling. If you want to combine them, things to consider include the following:\n"
"* Is DD applied consistently at all noise levels?\n"
"* Does folding preserve the DD structure?\n"
"* Does the resulting noise scaling still behave monotonically?\n"
msgstr ""
"El desacoplamiento dinámico (DD) es más matizado. DD altera dinámicamente el comportamiento del ruido cancelando parcialmente ciertos errores mediante la adición de secuencias de puertas. Si es posible construir los circuitos de modo que DD se comporte igual incluso cuando se pliegan puertas o bloques, en principio se podrían combinar ZNE y DD, pero en la práctica DD a veces interfiere con el escalado. Si quieres combinarlos, algunas cosas que debes considerar son las siguientes:\n"
"* ¿Se aplica DD de forma coherente en todos los niveles de ruido?\n"
"* ¿Conserva el plegado la estructura de DD?\n"
"* ¿Sigue comportándose el escalado de ruido resultante de forma monótona?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last error mitigation method we will discuss as a standalone approach is not compatible with ZNE: probabilistic error cancellation.\n"
msgstr "El último método de mitigación de errores que analizaremos como enfoque independiente no es compatible con ZNE: la cancelación probabilística de errores.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"
msgstr "Cancelación probabilística de errores (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike ZNE or measurement mitigation, PEC attempts to cancel noise at the gate level by reconstructing the ideal channel in expectation. Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) is the most powerful and most expensive error-mitigation technique covered in this lesson. PEC is built around explicit inversion of the noise channel, carried out statistically rather than physically. PEC works by:\n"
msgstr "A diferencia de ZNE o de la mitigación de mediciones, PEC intenta cancelar el ruido a nivel de puerta reconstruyendo el canal ideal en valor esperado. La cancelación probabilística de errores (PEC) es la técnica de mitigación de errores más potente y más costosa de las tratadas en esta lección. PEC se basa en la inversión explícita del canal de ruido, realizada de forma estadística y no física. PEC funciona de la siguiente manera:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise model in terms of a basis of \"error operations.\"\n"
msgstr "Caracteriza el modelo de ruido en términos de una base de \"operaciones de error\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressing the inverse of the noise channel as a quasi-probability distribution over physical operations.\n"
msgstr "Expresa la inversa del canal de ruido como una distribución de cuasi-probabilidad sobre operaciones físicas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling from this distribution during circuit execution to statistically construct an unbiased estimate of the ideal computation.\n"
msgstr "Muestrea de esta distribución durante la ejecución del circuito para construir estadísticamente una estimación insesgada del cálculo ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptually, PEC is like virtual error correction &mdash; it \"undoes\" noise by combining noisy operations in carefully weighted random patterns. Procedurally, however, PEC is not closely related to error correction or detection code. PEC's unbiased estimation of the ideal, noiseless expectation value comes at the cost of a very large sampling overhead and a strong dependence on accurate noise characterization.\n"
msgstr "Conceptualmente, PEC es como una corrección de errores virtual &mdash; \"deshace\" el ruido combinando operaciones ruidosas en patrones aleatorios cuidadosamente ponderados. Sin embargo, desde el punto de vista procedimental, PEC no está estrechamente relacionada con los códigos de corrección o detección de errores. La estimación insesgada que hace PEC del valor esperado ideal y sin ruido tiene el coste de una sobrecarga de muestreo muy grande y una fuerte dependencia de una caracterización precisa del ruido.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On IBM quantum computers, PEC is best viewed as a precision tool rather than a general-purpose mitigation layer: it is most appropriate for small circuits or small portions of larger circuits, benchmarking tasks, and high-accuracy studies where high quantum overhead is acceptable.\n"
msgstr "En los ordenadores cuánticos de IBM, PEC se considera mejor como una herramienta de precisión que como una capa de mitigación de propósito general: es más apropiada para circuitos pequeños o pequeñas porciones de circuitos más grandes, tareas de benchmarking y estudios de alta precisión en los que una sobrecarga cuántica elevada es aceptable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise channel {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Caracterización del canal de ruido {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In PEC, each ideal gate in a quantum circuit is modeled as an **ideal unitary channel** followed by a noise process. Let $\\rho$ denote the density matrix of the quantum state. The ideal gate is represented by a unitary matrix $U$, which induces a quantum channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"En PEC, cada puerta ideal de un circuito cuántico se modela como un **canal unitario ideal** seguido de un proceso de ruido. Sea $\\rho$ la matriz de densidad del estado cuántico. La puerta ideal se representa mediante una matriz unitaria $U$, que induce un canal cuántico:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On real hardware, this ideal evolution is corrupted by noise. We model the physical implementation of the gate as an **effective noisy channel**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\mathcal{N}$ is a noise channel capturing the stochastic errors associated with the gate. Throughout this discussion, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, and $\\mathcal{E}$ are linear maps acting on density operators. The ideal channel $\\mathcal{U}$ is unitary and reversible, while the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ (and hence $\\mathcal{E}$) is a completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP) map.\n"
msgstr ""
"En hardware real, esta evolución ideal se ve corrompida por el ruido. Modelamos la implementación física de la puerta como un **canal ruidoso efectivo**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"donde $\\mathcal{N}$ es un canal de ruido que captura los errores estocásticos asociados a la puerta. A lo largo de esta discusión, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$ y $\\mathcal{E}$ son aplicaciones lineales que actúan sobre operadores de densidad. El canal ideal $\\mathcal{U}$ es unitario y reversible, mientras que el canal de ruido $\\mathcal{N}$ (y por tanto $\\mathcal{E}$) es una aplicación completamente positiva que preserva la traza (CPTP).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC assumes that the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ is known or approximately known. On IBM Quantum hardware, this information is typically obtained from device calibration data, error rates inferred from benchmarking experiments, and simplified noise models such as Pauli or depolarizing approximations for small gate sets. While PEC does not require a perfectly accurate noise model, its performance degrades rapidly as the assumed noise channel diverges from the true hardware behavior.\n"
msgstr "PEC asume que el canal de ruido $\\mathcal{N}$ es conocido o aproximadamente conocido. En el hardware de IBM Quantum, esta información se obtiene normalmente a partir de datos de calibración del dispositivo, tasas de error inferidas de experimentos de benchmarking y modelos de ruido simplificados, como aproximaciones de Pauli o despolarizantes para conjuntos pequeños de puertas. Aunque PEC no requiere un modelo de ruido perfectamente exacto, su rendimiento se degrada rápidamente a medida que el canal de ruido asumido se aleja del comportamiento real del hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decomposition of the inverse noise channel {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Descomposición en cuasi-probabilidades del canal de ruido inverso {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The central idea of PEC is to **cancel the effect of noise in expectation** by constructing a stochastic approximation to the inverse of the noise channel. Formally, the goal is to apply a linear map that approximately undoes $\\mathcal{N}$, such that:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"in expectation over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"La idea central de PEC es **cancelar el efecto del ruido en valor esperado** construyendo una aproximación estocástica a la inversa del canal de ruido. Formalmente, el objetivo es aplicar una aplicación lineal que deshaga aproximadamente $\\mathcal{N}$, de modo que:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"en valor esperado sobre muchas ejecuciones del circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The inverse $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ is defined here as the algebraic inverse of $\\mathcal{N}$ treated as a linear superoperator acting on operators. This inverse exists only if $\\mathcal{N}$ is full-rank; non-invertible noise processes cannot be exactly mitigated using PEC.\n"
msgstr "La inversa $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ se define aquí como la inversa algebraica de $\\mathcal{N}$ tratada como un superoperador lineal que actúa sobre operadores. Esta inversa existe solo si $\\mathcal{N}$ es de rango completo; los procesos de ruido no invertibles no pueden mitigarse exactamente con PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When inversion is possible, PEC expresses the inverse noise channel as a **linear combination of physically implementable operations**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Here, each $\\mathcal{O}_i$ is a noisy operation that can be executed on the hardware (typically native gates or short gate sequences), and the real coefficients $\\eta_i$ form a **quasi-probability distribution**. Unlike ordinary probabilities, the coefficients $\\eta_i$ might be negative or exceed 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando la inversión es posible, PEC expresa el canal de ruido inverso como una **combinación lineal de operaciones físicamente implementables**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Aquí, cada $\\mathcal{O}_i$ es una operación ruidosa que se puede ejecutar en el hardware (normalmente puertas nativas o secuencias cortas de puertas), y los coeficientes reales $\\eta_i$ forman una **distribución de cuasi-probabilidad**. A diferencia de las probabilidades ordinarias, los coeficientes $\\eta_i$ pueden ser negativos o superar 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **quasi-probability norm**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"quantifies the cost of the noise inversion. For any nontrivial noise channel, $\\gamma > 1$. On IBM Quantum hardware, this decomposition is typically performed:\n"
"- per gate or per small gate set,\n"
"- assuming restricted noise models (often Pauli-diagonal approximations),\n"
"- using backend-specific native operations and scheduling constraints.\n"
msgstr ""
"La **norma de cuasi-probabilidad**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"cuantifica el coste de la inversión del ruido. Para cualquier canal de ruido no trivial, $\\gamma > 1$. En el hardware de IBM Quantum, esta descomposición se realiza normalmente:\n"
"- por puerta o por conjunto pequeño de puertas,\n"
"- asumiendo modelos de ruido restringidos (a menudo aproximaciones diagonales de Pauli),\n"
"- usando operaciones nativas específicas del backend y restricciones de planificación.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monte Carlo reconstruction of the ideal circuit {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"
msgstr "Reconstrucción Monte Carlo del circuito ideal {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To estimate the expectation value of an observable $O$, PEC uses Monte Carlo sampling based on the decomposition above. For each occurrence of a noisy gate in the circuit, the following procedure is applied:\n"
msgstr "Para estimar el valor esperado de un observable $O$, PEC usa muestreo Monte Carlo basado en la descomposición anterior. Para cada aparición de una puerta ruidosa en el circuito, se aplica el siguiente procedimiento:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Randomly select an operation $\\mathcal{O}_i$ with probability:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Selecciona aleatoriamente una operación $\\mathcal{O}_i$ con probabilidad:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assign a classical weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Asigna un peso clásico:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the resulting randomized noisy circuit on the quantum backend.\n"
msgstr "Ejecuta el circuito ruidoso aleatorizado resultante en el backend cuántico.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the measured outcome by the product of all accumulated weights.\n"
msgstr "Multiplica el resultado medido por el producto de todos los pesos acumulados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Average the weighted results over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr "Promedia los resultados ponderados sobre muchas ejecuciones del circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The resulting estimator $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ satisfies\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"provided the noise model $\\mathcal{N}$ accurately describes the hardware. PEC therefore introduces **no systematic bias** in expectation, but replaces bias with **large statistical variance**. Each run produces a noisy but weighted estimate; only after averaging many such runs does the ideal expectation value emerge.\n"
msgstr ""
"El estimador resultante $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ satisface\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"siempre que el modelo de ruido $\\mathcal{N}$ describa con exactitud el hardware. Por lo tanto, PEC no introduce **ningún sesgo sistemático** en valor esperado, pero sustituye el sesgo por una **gran varianza estadística**. Cada ejecución produce una estimación ruidosa pero ponderada; solo tras promediar muchas de estas ejecuciones emerge el valor esperado ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual interpretation {#conceptual-interpretation}"
msgstr "Interpretación conceptual {#conceptual-interpretation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is sometimes described as *virtual error correction*. While this phrasing is not entirely incorrect, it should not be confused with true quantum error correction. PEC involves no logical encoding, no syndrome extraction, and no real-time feedback. Errors are not prevented or corrected during circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "A veces se describe PEC como *corrección de errores virtual*. Aunque esta expresión no es del todo incorrecta, no debe confundirse con la verdadera corrección cuántica de errores. PEC no implica codificación lógica, ni extracción de síndromes, ni retroalimentación en tiempo real. Los errores no se previenen ni se corrigen durante la ejecución del circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead, PEC cancels noise **statistically**, by combining many noisy circuit realizations with signed classical weights so that errors cancel only after classical post-processing. Information is not protected during execution; ideal results are reconstructed after the fact.\n"
msgstr "En cambio, PEC cancela el ruido **estadísticamente**, combinando muchas realizaciones ruidosas del circuito con pesos clásicos con signo, de modo que los errores se cancelan solo tras el posprocesamiento clásico. La información no se protege durante la ejecución; los resultados ideales se reconstruyen a posteriori.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resource scaling and cost {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"
msgstr "Escalado de recursos y coste {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dominant cost of PEC stems from variance amplification. The variance of the PEC estimator scales as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"implying:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Required number of shots} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"El coste dominante de PEC proviene de la amplificación de la varianza. La varianza del estimador de PEC escala como:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"lo que implica:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Número de shots necesarios} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This scaling is fundamental and cannot be improved through classical post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Este escalado es fundamental y no se puede mejorar mediante posprocesamiento clásico.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For circuits containing many noisy gates, each gate contributes a factor $\\gamma_k > 1$, causing the total quasi-probability norm to grow approximately multiplicatively:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d$ is the circuit depth. On IBM Quantum hardware, this typically leads to exponential growth in sampling cost with circuit depth, with particularly strong sensitivity to two-qubit gate errors. This scaling places practical limits on the applicability of PEC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para circuitos con muchas puertas ruidosas, cada puerta aporta un factor $\\gamma_k > 1$, lo que hace que la norma de cuasi-probabilidad total crezca aproximadamente de forma multiplicativa:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"donde $d$ es la profundidad del circuito. En el hardware de IBM Quantum, esto suele provocar un crecimiento exponencial del coste de muestreo con la profundidad del circuito, con una sensibilidad especialmente fuerte a los errores de las puertas de dos qubits. Este escalado impone límites prácticos a la aplicabilidad de PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is currently practical only when one or all of the following conditions are met:\n"
msgstr "Actualmente PEC solo es práctica cuando se cumplen una o todas las siguientes condiciones:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuits are very small or shallow (often $\\leq 10-20$ gates),\n"
msgstr "Los circuitos son muy pequeños o poco profundos (a menudo $\\leq 10-20$ puertas),\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise models are simple and well-validated (for example, Pauli noise),\n"
msgstr "Los modelos de ruido son simples y están bien validados (por ejemplo, ruido de Pauli),\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High statistical cost is acceptable,\n"
msgstr "Un coste estadístico alto es aceptable,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The goal is accuracy rather than throughput.\n"
msgstr "El objetivo es la precisión y no el rendimiento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this reason, PEC is often applied to:\n"
msgstr "Por este motivo, PEC se aplica a menudo a:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Isolated subcircuits within larger workflows,\n"
msgstr "Subcircuitos aislados dentro de flujos de trabajo más grandes,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short-time evolution steps,\n"
msgstr "Pasos de evolución de tiempo corto,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "State preparation or measurement routines,\n"
msgstr "Rutinas de preparación de estados o de medición,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarking and validation experiments.\n"
msgstr "Experimentos de benchmarking y validación.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IBM software stack (IBM Quantum Compute and error-mitigation tooling) reflects this by treating PEC as a specialized option, not a default mitigation layer.\n"
msgstr "El stack de software de IBM (IBM Quantum Compute y las herramientas de mitigación de errores) lo refleja tratando PEC como una opción especializada, no como una capa de mitigación predeterminada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical PEC use cases include:\n"
msgstr "Los casos de uso típicos de PEC incluyen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Precision benchmarking of quantum hardware,\n"
msgstr "Evaluación comparativa de precisión del hardware cuántico,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification of small quantum algorithms,\n"
msgstr "Verificación de algoritmos cuánticos pequeños,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-accuracy quantum chemistry on reduced systems,\n"
msgstr "Química cuántica de alta precisión en sistemas reducidos,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-checking ZNE or other mitigation methods.\n"
msgstr "Verificación cruzada de ZNE u otros métodos de mitigación.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC's relationship to other mitigation methods {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"
msgstr "Relación de PEC con otros métodos de mitigación {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many other mitigation techniques trade accuracy for scalability; PEC does just the opposite, focusing on accuracy above all else.\n"
msgstr "Muchas otras técnicas de mitigación sacrifican precisión a cambio de escalabilidad; PEC hace justo lo contrario, y se centra en la precisión por encima de todo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because PEC might only be used on a subcircuit, it is especially important here to ask what other mitigation methods can be combined with it. To reason clearly about compatibility with PEC, it helps to categorize techniques by what they do to the noise. Consider these general categories:\n"
msgstr "Dado que PEC puede usarse solo en un subcircuito, aquí es especialmente importante preguntarse qué otros métodos de mitigación pueden combinarse con él. Para razonar con claridad sobre la compatibilidad con PEC, conviene clasificar las técnicas según lo que hacen con el ruido. Considera estas categorías generales:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise cancellation - attempt to invert error channels\n"
msgstr "Cancelación de ruido: intentan invertir los canales de error\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise scaling - deliberately increase noise to extrapolate\n"
msgstr "Escalado de ruido: aumentan deliberadamente el ruido para extrapolar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise reshaping - change the structure or spectrum of noise\n"
msgstr "Remodelación del ruido: cambian la estructura o el espectro del ruido\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bias removal - correct errors that do not scale with gate noise\n"
msgstr "Eliminación de sesgo: corrigen errores que no escalan con el ruido de las puertas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC sits squarely in category (1). Any method that changes or rescales the noise channel must be examined carefully.\n"
msgstr "PEC se sitúa claramente en la categoría (1). Cualquier método que cambie o reescale el canal de ruido debe examinarse con cuidado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary table (high-level)\n"
msgstr "Tabla resumen (nivel general)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Technique | Compatible with PEC | Notes |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | No | Undoing versus scaling and sometimes tailoring error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Yes (with care) | Affects error behavior, but might make it easier to learn |\n"
"| TREX | Yes | No overlap in workflow. Fully compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Usually no | Changes error channel |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Técnica | Compatible con PEC | Notas |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | No | Deshacer frente a escalar y, a veces, adaptar el error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Sí (con cuidado) | Afecta al comportamiento del error, pero puede facilitar su aprendizaje |\n"
"| TREX | Sí | Sin solapamiento en el flujo de trabajo. Totalmente compatible. |\n"
"|Desacoplamiento dinámico | Normalmente no | Cambia el canal de error |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and ZNE address the same error sources (gate errors) via mutually incompatible assumptions or workstreams, or both. For example, in ZNE, we assume error can be expanded in a parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"and that the error can be effectively scaled to model this expansion. PEC would undo the very error we rely on for the scaling. The parameter $\\lambda$ would become meaningless. Another way of thinking about it is:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC y ZNE abordan las mismas fuentes de error (errores de las puertas) mediante supuestos o flujos de trabajo mutuamente incompatibles, o ambos. Por ejemplo, en ZNE suponemos que el error puede expandirse en un parámetro $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"y que el error puede escalarse de forma efectiva para modelar esta expansión. PEC desharía precisamente el error en el que nos apoyamos para el escalado. El parámetro $\\lambda$ perdería todo sentido. Otra forma de verlo es:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying ZNE before PEC changes the noise channel you are trying to invert.\n"
msgstr "Aplicar ZNE antes de PEC cambia el canal de ruido que intentas invertir.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC before ZNE removes the very noise ZNE relies on to extrapolate.\n"
msgstr "Aplicar PEC antes de ZNE elimina justo el ruido en el que ZNE se apoya para extrapolar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC and ZNE should be considered alternative error-mitigation paradigms, not composable layers. Comparing them side-by-side is instructive, while combining them is not.\n"
msgstr "PEC y ZNE deben considerarse paradigmas alternativos de mitigación de errores, no capas componibles. Compararlos lado a lado resulta instructivo, mientras que combinarlos no.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and Pauli twirling are generally compatible and often beneficial.\n"
"Twirling might help PEC in that twirling converts coherent errors into stochastic Pauli errors. This simplifies the noise channel, making it easier to represent and invert. For PEC, this is extremely valuable, for the following reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC y Pauli twirling son generalmente compatibles y a menudo beneficiosos.\n"
"El twirling puede ayudar a PEC porque convierte los errores coherentes en errores de Pauli estocásticos. Esto simplifica el canal de ruido y facilita su representación e inversión. Para PEC esto es extremadamente valioso, por las siguientes razones:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decompositions are much simpler for Pauli channels\n"
msgstr "Las descomposiciones en cuasi-probabilidades son mucho más simples para los canales de Pauli\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quasi-probability norm $\\gamma$ is often significantly smaller\n"
msgstr "La norma de cuasi-probabilidad $\\gamma$ suele ser significativamente menor\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling variance is reduced\n"
msgstr "Se reduce la varianza del muestreo\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many PEC demonstrations assume or build in Pauli-twirled noise.\n"
"It's important to clarify that Pauli twirling does not mitigate errors by itself; it reshapes noise into a form that probabilistic error cancellation can handle more efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Muchas demostraciones de PEC suponen o incorporan ruido sometido a Pauli twirling.\n"
"Es importante aclarar que el Pauli twirling no mitiga los errores por sí mismo; remodela el ruido en una forma que la cancelación probabilística de errores puede manejar con mayor eficiencia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC can and should be combined with TREX. These approaches are fully compatible and play orthogonal roles. TREX operates only at measurement, removes readout bias via randomized twirls of the measurement channel, and does not affect gate noise or circuit dynamics. PEC operates on gate noise. Because measurement error is additive rather than compositional, it is independent of gate sequences. It is safe and often desirable to apply TREX alongside PEC.\n"
msgstr "PEC puede y debe combinarse con TREX. Estos enfoques son totalmente compatibles y desempeñan funciones ortogonales. TREX opera solo en la medición, elimina el sesgo de lectura mediante twirls aleatorizados del canal de medición, y no afecta al ruido de las puertas ni a la dinámica del circuito. PEC opera sobre el ruido de las puertas. Como el error de medición es aditivo y no composicional, es independiente de las secuencias de puertas. Es seguro, y a menudo deseable, aplicar TREX junto con PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering of these methods is what you might expect:\n"
"1. Execute PEC-randomized circuit\n"
"2. Apply TREX to mitigate readout error\n"
"3. Apply PEC weighting and averaging\n"
msgstr ""
"El orden de estos métodos es el que cabría esperar:\n"
"1. Ejecutar el circuito aleatorizado de PEC\n"
"2. Aplicar TREX para mitigar el error de lectura\n"
"3. Aplicar la ponderación y el promedio de PEC\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and DD are generally incompatible unless the noise characterization used for PEC is performed with DD active. PEC assumes that $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"is stationary, repeatable, and accurately characterizable. DD explicitly reshapes the noise channel in time by modulating system-environment interactions and introducing non-trivial pulse-timing effects. As a result, the effective noise with DD is not the same channel as without DD. This is made even more complex by the fact that the noise channel can depend sensitively on circuit scheduling. The end result is that noise inversion becomes ill-defined or invalid.\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC y DD son generalmente incompatibles, a menos que la caracterización del ruido usada para PEC se realice con DD activo. PEC supone que $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"es estacionario, repetible y caracterizable con precisión. DD remodela explícitamente el canal de ruido en el tiempo al modular las interacciones sistema-entorno e introducir efectos no triviales de temporización de pulsos. Como resultado, el ruido efectivo con DD no es el mismo canal que sin DD. Esto se complica aún más porque el canal de ruido puede depender de manera sensible de la planificación del circuito. El resultado final es que la inversión del ruido queda mal definida o es inválida.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is theoretically possible to characterize noise with DD active and build a PEC model accordingly, but this is highly advanced and not currently a recommended workflow.\n"
msgstr "En teoría es posible caracterizar el ruido con DD activo y construir un modelo de PEC en consecuencia, pero esto es muy avanzado y actualmente no es un flujo de trabajo recomendado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC by hand {#applying-pec-by-hand}"
msgstr "Aplicar PEC a mano {#applying-pec-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is complex and it is not recommended that you implement it by hand. Still, we want to work through the math of a basic application on a single qubit to understand what steps the process entails. We choose a mixed but nontrivial state so that we can see numerical effects clearly.\n"
msgstr "PEC es complejo y no se recomienda implementarlo a mano. Aun así, queremos desarrollar las matemáticas de una aplicación básica sobre un solo qubit para entender qué pasos implica el proceso. Elegimos un estado mixto pero no trivial para poder ver con claridad los efectos numéricos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Take a qubit that should be in the pure state\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Toma un qubit que debería estar en el estado puro\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ideal density matrix is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"La matriz de densidad ideal es:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"We've chosen this density matrix because it is not diagonal and is only for a single qubit so that it is tractable to examine \"by hand\".\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Hemos elegido esta matriz de densidad porque no es diagonal y es solo para un único qubit, de modo que resulta manejable examinarla \"a mano\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now apply a very simple, but realistic noise model: a single-qubit depolarizing channel, with small strength $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora aplicamos un modelo de ruido muy simple pero realista: un canal despolarizante de un solo qubit, con una intensidad pequeña $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep the arithmetic friendly, take $p = 0.15$. This channel is completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP), as it must be. It is a realistic noise channel for real hardware, or at least realistic for describing some of the noise. Further, this noise channel is analytically invertible, as a linear map. In other words, there exists an inverse matrix, but that doesn't mean that the matrix corresponds to a CPTP physical channel, and it certainly doesn't correspond to a unitary that could be implemented on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Para que la aritmética sea amigable, toma $p = 0.15$. Este canal es completamente positivo y conserva la traza (CPTP), como debe ser. Es un canal de ruido realista para hardware real, o al menos realista para describir parte del ruido. Además, este canal de ruido es analíticamente invertible, como aplicación lineal. En otras palabras, existe una matriz inversa, pero eso no significa que la matriz corresponda a un canal físico CPTP, y desde luego no corresponde a un unitario que pueda implementarse en hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we apply our depolarizing noise channel to our single-qubit density matrix and obtain:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"With $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ and $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora aplicamos nuestro canal de ruido despolarizante a nuestra matriz de densidad de un solo qubit y obtenemos:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"Con $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ y $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying this to our state:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicando esto a nuestro estado:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute explicitly:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Calculamos explícitamente:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"This is still a physical density matrix, and it still has trace one &mdash; but it is more mixed now.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(redondeado)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Esta sigue siendo una matriz de densidad física y todavía tiene traza uno &mdash; pero ahora está más mezclada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we compute the ideal inverse channel, but being very prepared for the possibility that it might not be physical. We will check whether it is. Mathematically, the inverse linear map is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora calculamos el canal inverso ideal, pero muy preparados para la posibilidad de que no sea físico. Comprobaremos si lo es. Matemáticamente, la aplicación lineal inversa es:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If this inverse action were itself a valid physical channel, then we would be tempted to try to implement it exactly. Of course, we would still need to figure out how to implement it using unitary operations and classical steps, but implementing this would be the goal. However, it turns out this is *not* CPTP, and there is generally no guarantee that such inverse mappings will be CPTP. That is critical to our current discussion, because it is the reason PEC exists.\n"
msgstr "Si esta acción inversa fuera en sí misma un canal físico válido, nos sentiríamos tentados a intentar implementarla exactamente. Por supuesto, aún tendríamos que averiguar cómo implementarla mediante operaciones unitarias y pasos clásicos, pero ese sería el objetivo. Sin embargo, resulta que esto *no* es CPTP, y en general no hay garantía de que tales aplicaciones inversas sean CPTP. Eso es crítico para nuestra discusión actual, porque es la razón por la que existe PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might be able to see that it is not CPTP just by looking at it. A sure-fire check is to apply it to a density matrix and see if it returns physical results. This is left as an exercise to check your understanding.\n"
msgstr "Quizá puedas ver que no es CPTP con solo mirarlo. Una comprobación infalible es aplicarlo a una matriz de densidad y ver si devuelve resultados físicos. Esto se deja como ejercicio para comprobar tu comprensión.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Comprueba tu comprensión {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether the inverse mapping from above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ is CPTP by applying it to a new density matrix:\n"
msgstr "Comprueba si la aplicación inversa anterior $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ es CPTP aplicándola a una nueva matriz de densidad:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results as being physical or non-physical.\n"
msgstr "Interpreta los resultados como físicos o no físicos.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a physical density matrix, this corresponds to a classical probability of greater than 1 that the system is in the state $|0\\rangle$ and a negative probability of being in the state $|1\\rangle$. Clearly this mapping can yield nonsense density matrices. Further, by inspection we can see that the eigenvalues of the resulting density matrix are 1.0625 and -0.0625, meaning not all eigenvalues are positive. Thus the mapping is not \"completely positive\", the \"CP\" in CPTP.\n"
msgstr "Como matriz de densidad física, esto corresponde a una probabilidad clásica mayor que 1 de que el sistema esté en el estado $|0\\rangle$ y a una probabilidad negativa de estar en el estado $|1\\rangle$. Claramente, esta aplicación puede producir matrices de densidad sin sentido. Además, por inspección podemos ver que los valores propios de la matriz de densidad resultante son 1.0625 y -0.0625, lo que significa que no todos los valores propios son positivos. Por lo tanto, la aplicación no es \"completamente positiva\", la \"CP\" de CPTP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check by explicit calculation that the inverse operation above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ undoes the noise channel and returns the noise-free state.\n"
msgstr "Comprueba mediante un cálculo explícito que la operación inversa anterior $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ deshace el canal de ruido y devuelve el estado libre de ruido.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it to the noisy state:\n"
msgstr "Aplícala al estado con ruido:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is exactly the original state (up to rounding).\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Este es exactamente el estado original (salvo redondeo).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We restate to be absolutely clear: we cannot invert the noise channel exactly; the inverse is not CPTP, nor is it a valid physical channel. However, we can effectively invert the channel as a linear combination of physical channels.\n"
msgstr "Lo repetimos para que quede absolutamente claro: no podemos invertir el canal de ruido exactamente; la inversa no es CPTP, ni es un canal físico válido. Sin embargo, sí podemos invertir el canal de forma efectiva como una combinación lineal de canales físicos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"where: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para el canal despolarizante:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"donde: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ etc.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The inverse can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"La inversa puede escribirse como:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with:\n"
msgstr "with:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = physically implementable Clifford channels\n"
msgstr "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = canales de Clifford físicamente implementables\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilities\n"
msgstr "$\\eta_j$ = cuasi-probabilidades\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "Esta es la idea central de PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Muestrear canales según $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Asignar signos a los resultados de medición\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Los valores esperados convergen al valor libre de ruido\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Aplicamos PEC \"a mano\" a la estimación de $\\langle Z \\rangle$ usando la matriz de densidad $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ y vemos si podemos recuperar los resultados de $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Para $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ esperamos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Observa también que, para la matriz de densidad con ruido, obtenemos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "Tiene el orden de magnitud correcto, pero está significativamente lejos del caso ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Ahora vemos paso a paso cómo, con el proceso de PEC, podemos reconstruir el valor esperado sin sesgo a partir de la matriz de densidad con ruido. En los flujos de trabajo reales, esto es probabilístico y se automatiza. En este flujo \"a mano\" elegiremos valores probabilísticos que son realistas, pero quizá convenientes para nuestra presentación. Esto no debe interpretarse como una afirmación de que PEC sea perfecto. Es simplemente para mostrarte un escenario plausible que podría ocurrir dentro de los paquetes de PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que nuestro canal de ruido tiene la forma:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"La inversa puede escribirse (exactamente):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Para esta introducción es más simple centrarse en el efecto del canal sobre nuestra matriz de densidad. Esto nos permite trabajar con objetos familiares como las matrices de densidad y los valores esperados. Con ese fin, considera qué debe cumplirse sobre los efectos de esta operación inversa en nuestro proceso de estimación: el estimador producido por PEC debe estar normalizado y no tener sesgo. Esto corresponde a dos condiciones:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalización: para asegurar que esta operación no cambie la escala del observable, exigimos que $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Para ver por qué ocurre esto, podríamos considerar la acción de la inversa sobre una matriz de densidad, o su acción sobre el valor esperado de algo trivial como el propio $\\mathcal{I}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Calibración: en un flujo de trabajo real, usamos circuitos de calibración para aprender el comportamiento del ruido a nivel de puerta. Luego usamos ese conocimiento a nivel de puerta y la linealidad de los valores esperados para aplicar el modelo de ruido aprendido al circuito más grande. En nuestro caso, partimos del conocimiento artificial de que el valor esperado ideal es $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Pero sería muy fácil idear un estado para el que sepamos teóricamente que este sería el valor ideal, y luego usar mediciones reales para la calibración. Un punto clave es que, en PEC, normalmente no se aprende un modelo de ruido completo de todo el circuito. En su lugar, se aprenden modelos de ruido locales para puertas individuales o capas del circuito y se usan para construir la descomposición en cuasi-probabilidades.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Usamos estas condiciones para determinar $\\alpha$ y $\\beta$. Consideramos el ansatz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que los canales de Pauli actúan por conjugación:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicar $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ a $\\rho$ da:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tomando la traza, obtenemos:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada operador de Pauli es unitario, por lo que la conjugación conserva la traza:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Para que el estimador de PEC esté normalizado, la aplicación\n"
"inversa efectiva debe conservar la traza de todas las matrices de densidad. Es decir, exigimos:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{para todo } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto implica la restricción de normalización:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "Pero en nuestro caso, esto da la condición:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Ahora usamos la información de calibración para relacionar el valor esperado observado con el ideal conocido.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving our two conditions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Resolviendo nuestras dos condiciones para $\\alpha$ y $\\beta$, obtenemos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These coefficients sum to 1, but one of them is negative.\n"
msgstr "Estos coeficientes suman 1, pero uno de ellos es negativo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can recover the ideal expectation value by randomly modifying the circuit, measuring, multiplying the result by a signed weight, and averaging. In particular, no density matrices are reconstructed and no inverse channel is implemented physically.\n"
msgstr "Podemos recuperar el valor esperado ideal modificando el circuito de forma aleatoria, midiendo, multiplicando el resultado por un peso con signo y promediando. En particular, no se reconstruye ninguna matriz de densidad ni se implementa físicamente ningún canal inverso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key step: this is PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"
msgstr "El paso clave: esto es PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our noise strength $p=0.15$, the inverse channel can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para nuestra intensidad de ruido $p=0.15$, el canal inverso puede escribirse como:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important facts:\n"
msgstr "Hechos importantes:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients sum to 1\n"
msgstr "Los coeficientes suman 1\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "One coefficient is negative\n"
msgstr "Un coeficiente es negativo\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each term is physically implementable\n"
msgstr "Cada término es físicamente implementable\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The negativity moves into classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "La negatividad pasa al posprocesamiento clásico\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We form a sampling distribution from the absolute values of the weights:\n"
msgstr "Formamos una distribución de muestreo a partir de los valores absolutos de los pesos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(for each of X, Y, Z)\n"
msgstr "(para cada uno de X, Y, Z)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Total weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Peso total:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For sampling probabilities, divide by W.\n"
msgstr "Para obtener las probabilidades de muestreo, divide entre W.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Operation | Probability | Sign |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Do nothing ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Apply X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Operación | Probabilidad | Signo |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| No hacer nada ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Aplicar X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Aplicar Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Aplicar Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sign comes from the original coefficient, not the probability.\n"
msgstr "El signo proviene del coeficiente original, no de la probabilidad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each shot consists of these steps:\n"
msgstr "Cada shot consta de estos pasos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the state\n"
msgstr "Preparar el estado\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the hardware apply the noisy circuit\n"
msgstr "Dejar que el hardware aplique el circuito con ruido\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomly choose an operation from the table above using the associated probabilities\n"
msgstr "Elegir aleatoriamente una operación de la tabla anterior usando las probabilidades asociadas\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it\n"
msgstr "Apply it\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure $Z$, getting $\\pm 1$\n"
msgstr "Medir $Z$, obteniendo $\\pm 1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the outcome by $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"
msgstr "Multiplicar el resultado por $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Record that number\n"
msgstr "Registrar ese número\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now do examples of several shots.\n"
msgstr "Ahora veamos ejemplos de varios shots.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 1 (identity case)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 1 (caso de la identidad)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose our randomly chosen operation is the identity $\\mathcal{I}$ (or equivalently: do nothing). Based on the arguments and the table above, this will happen 86.4% of the time. Because the coefficient of $\\mathcal{I}$ in the inverse of the noise channel is positive, we select the $+$ sign. Our measurement of Z could easily yield either $\\pm 1$. Let us suppose it yields $+1$.\n"
msgstr "Supongamos que nuestra operación elegida al azar es la identidad $\\mathcal{I}$ (o, equivalentemente: no hacer nada). Según los argumentos y la tabla anteriores, esto ocurrirá el 86.4% de las veces. Como el coeficiente de $\\mathcal{I}$ en la inversa del canal de ruido es positivo, seleccionamos el signo $+$. Nuestra medición de Z podría dar fácilmente $\\pm 1$. Supongamos que da $+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The PEC-corrected contribution from this shot would be:\n"
"$(+1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375$\n"
msgstr ""
"La contribución corregida por PEC de este shot sería:\n"
"$(+1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 2 (identity again)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 2 (de nuevo la identidad)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose we again obtain $\\mathcal{I}$ as our random operation (so the sign of the term is initially still $+$), but this time our measurement of Z yields $-1$. This time the contribution is:\n"
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que de nuevo obtenemos $\\mathcal{I}$ como operación aleatoria (por lo que el signo del término sigue siendo inicialmente $+$), pero esta vez nuestra medición de Z da $-1$. Esta vez la contribución es:\n"
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 3 (X chosen)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 3 (se elige X)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This time our random operation is X. This term in the inverse is negative, so we keep a $-$ sign. We apply X and then measure Z. Again, we could obtain either eigenvalue; say we obtain $-1$. The contribution from this term is:\n"
msgstr "Esta vez nuestra operación aleatoria es X. Este término en la inversa es negativo, así que mantenemos un signo $-$. Aplicamos X y luego medimos Z. De nuevo, podríamos obtener cualquiera de los dos valores propios; digamos que obtenemos $-1$. La contribución de este término es:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 4 (Z chosen)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 4 (se elige Z)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The random operation is Z. This gives us a $-$ sign from the table. Suppose we measure Z and obtain $+1$. The contribution is:\n"
msgstr "La operación aleatoria es Z. Esto nos da un signo $-$ según la tabla. Supongamos que medimos Z y obtenemos $+1$. La contribución es:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(+1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(+1) \\times (-1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 5 (Y chosen)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 5 (se elige Y)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The random operation is Y. This gives us a $-$ sign from the table. Suppose we measure Z and obtain $+1$. The contribution is:\n"
msgstr "La operación aleatoria es Y. Esto nos da un signo $-$ según la tabla. Supongamos que medimos Z y obtenemos $+1$. La contribución es:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Averaging the results**\n"
msgstr "**Promedio de los resultados**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Imagine we collect many such PEC-weighted outcomes:\n"
msgstr "Imagina que recopilamos muchos resultados ponderados por PEC como estos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{ +1.375,-1.375,+1.375,-1.375,-1.375,\\dots \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{ +1.375,-1.375,+1.375,-1.375,-1.375,\\dots \\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By construction, we apply the identity 86.4% of the time. We apply each of the other gates 4.5% of the time. In a real workflow, we don't know the precise underlying states, nor the entire noise channel. But we do know the weighting factor $W \\equiv 1.375$ from above, and the relative probability with which we apply each operation. In a real workflow, we rely on the unknown density matrix to give us measurement outcomes. We will verify here that this procedure would yield the correct results.\n"
msgstr "Por construcción, aplicamos la identidad el 86.4% de las veces. Aplicamos cada una de las otras puertas el 4.5% de las veces. En un flujo de trabajo real, no conocemos los estados subyacentes precisos, ni todo el canal de ruido. Pero sí conocemos el factor de ponderación $W \\equiv 1.375$ de arriba, y la probabilidad relativa con la que aplicamos cada operación. En un flujo de trabajo real, dependemos de la matriz de densidad desconocida para obtener los resultados de medición. Aquí verificaremos que este procedimiento daría los resultados correctos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to calculate the average of all weighted, signed measurements including applications of Pauli operators $P_i$ prior to measurement. Call the total number of all shots $N_\\text{shots}$. Call the set of all shots for which Pauli $P_i$ was applied $S_{P_i}$ and use $j$ to index these shots. Call the measurement outcome of the $j^\\text{th}$ shot under the application of the $i^\\text{th}$ Pauli $z_{ij}$. We can write this average as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC} = \\frac{W}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{i\\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}} \\text{sign}_i \\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\n"
"$$\n"
"The Pauli operator $P_i$ is applied probabilistically with probability $p_i$. In the limit of a large number of shots,\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\text{Number of shots with Pauli } P_i \\text{ applied}}{N_\\text{shots}}\n"
"$$\n"
"We can use this to write:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{z_{i,j}} & = \\frac{p_i}{N_{\\text{shots with }P_i}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\\\\\n"
"&  = p_i \\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}$ is the expectation value of Z only over the ensemble of shots in which $P_i$ was applied. This is useful because we know what each such expectation value must be from the density matrix. Again, in a real workflow, this would emerge from measurement, not from a known density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{I} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZI\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}I\\right) = 0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{X} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZX\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}X\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Y} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZY\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Y\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Z} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZZ\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Z\\right) = 0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Queremos calcular el promedio de todas las mediciones ponderadas y con signo, incluyendo las aplicaciones de operadores de Pauli $P_i$ antes de la medición. Llama $N_\\text{shots}$ al número total de shots. Llama $S_{P_i}$ al conjunto de todos los shots en los que se aplicó el Pauli $P_i$ y usa $j$ para indexar esos shots. Llama $z_{ij}$ al resultado de medición del $j$-ésimo shot bajo la aplicación del $i$-ésimo Pauli. Podemos escribir este promedio como:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC} = \\frac{W}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{i\\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}} \\text{sign}_i \\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\n"
"$$\n"
"El operador de Pauli $P_i$ se aplica de forma probabilística con probabilidad $p_i$. En el límite de un gran número de shots,\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\text{Number of shots with Pauli } P_i \\text{ applied}}{N_\\text{shots}}\n"
"$$\n"
"Podemos usar esto para escribir:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{N_\\text{shots}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{z_{i,j}} & = \\frac{p_i}{N_{\\text{shots with }P_i}}\\sum_{j\\in S_{P_i}}{ z_{i,j}}\\\\\n"
"&  = p_i \\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"donde $\\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}$ es el valor esperado de Z solo sobre el conjunto de shots en los que se aplicó $P_i$. Esto es útil porque sabemos cuál debe ser cada uno de estos valores esperados a partir de la matriz de densidad. De nuevo, en un flujo de trabajo real, esto surgiría de la medición, no de una matriz de densidad conocida.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{I} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZI\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}I\\right) = 0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{X} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZX\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}X\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Y} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZY\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Y\\right) = -0.4\\\\\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_{Z} & = \\text{Tr}\\left(ZZ\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}Z\\right) = 0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

